# Code cleanliness

- Never leave unused variables, imports, function parameters, or destructured props.
- Delete unused values. Do not prefix with `_`, comment them out, or disable lint to hide them.
- Only destructure props you actually use.
- Before finishing, re-scan the diff for anything declared but never referenced.

# Build is the definition of done

- This project builds with `npm run build` (Next.js + TypeScript + ESLint). ESLint errors fail production builds on Vercel.
- Treat `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`, `no-undef`, TypeScript errors, and other lint/type errors as build-breaking bugs.
- Do not call a feature finished if it would fail `npm run build`. If the change is untested against the build, say so explicitly.

# Third-party / copied components

- Do not paste library snippets (smoothui, unlumen-ui, shadcn, etc.) wholesale.
- Strip unused props, imports, and dead variables as part of integrating them.
- Keep only what this project actually uses.

# TypeScript / Next.js

- Prefer deleting dead code over `eslint-disable`. Use a disable only with a genuine, stated reason.
- Keep types accurate. Do not use `any` to bypass type errors.
- Do not add new npm dependencies unless the task requires them, and flag it when you do.

```tsx
// BAD
function Card({ title, unused }: { title: string; unused: string }) {
  return <h3>{title}</h3>;
}

// GOOD
function Card({ title }: { title: string }) {
  return <h3>{title}</h3>;
}
```
